# Day 28

**18km / 5 hours**

Decided to have a shorter day so I could take my time today. Wanted to get out of the city centre as soon as reasonable so after getting packed up I made my way on the trail. 

Following the trail through the city centre is a bit odd; you feel out of place amongst the regular people going about their day. Especially since the trail has a section going through the university campus and other populated streets. Still cities are strange places with many strange people so you can get on with the walk. 

The trail definitely takes a more scenic option over a direct route in this city, trying to hit a few parks and pleasant areas. They're cool enough I suppose. The views of the city are alright. 

![The view of Auckland from one of the hills along the way](./auckland-view.jpg)

After a while the trail crossed a bridge and became less populated as it escaped the nucleus of the city. This was more parks and some coastal areas that I passed without much incident but I will mention that the toilet facilities were weirdly high tech with a voice that tells you how to use the facilities which is very creepy, almost as if it were modelled off a dystopian movie.

Coming to the campsite relatively early even though I tried to take my time with the walk I got to help out with some small activities and look around the farm nearby. It's more of a show farm for school children and groups to look at which is nice. It has a large mix of animals, from chickens and sheep to pigs and goats.

![Some young goats at the farm](./baby-goats.jpg)